## Install on 9front

### Option A: install-go.rc (recommended)

One-shot installer that downloads the tarball for `$objtype`, verifies
its sha256, restarts `webfs`, and extracts into `$goroot` (default
`/sys/lib/go`).

Fresh install (no existing `/sys/lib/go`):

```
% hget @@BASE_URL@@/install-go.rc | rc
```

With flags (`-y` to back up and replace an existing install, custom
`-goroot`, etc.).  9front rc has no `--` flag-end; pipe into the dot
builtin so the script sees the positional args:

```
% hget @@BASE_URL@@/install-go.rc | rc -c '. /fd/0 -y'
% hget @@BASE_URL@@/install-go.rc | rc -c '. /fd/0 -y -goroot $home/go'
```

Or, fetch first if you want to read it before running:

```
% hget @@BASE_URL@@/install-go.rc > /tmp/install-go.rc
% rc /tmp/install-go.rc -y
```

Available flags:

- `-base URL`     override the download root (default `@@BASE_URL@@`)
- `-goroot DIR`   override the install location (default `/sys/lib/go`)
- `-arch ARCH`    override `$objtype` (`amd64` or `arm64`)
- `-y`            non-interactive: back up any existing `$goroot`

### Option B: manual

Pick the tarball matching `$objtype` (`amd64` or `arm64`):

```
% cd /sys/lib
% hget @@BASE_URL@@/go-plan9-$objtype.tar.gz | gunzip | tar x
% bind -bc /sys/lib/go/bin /$objtype/bin
% GOROOT=/sys/lib/go go version
```

### After install

To make `go` available in every shell, add to `$home/lib/profile`:

```
GOROOT=/sys/lib/go
path=($path /sys/lib/go/bin)
```

## Verify

```
% hget @@BASE_URL@@/SHA256SUMS > /tmp/SHA256SUMS
% sha1sum -2 256 go-plan9-$objtype.tar.gz
% grep go-plan9-$objtype.tar.gz /tmp/SHA256SUMS
```

The two sha256 hex strings must match.

## Tarball layout

Each archive expands to a single top-level `go/` directory (upstream
convention):

```
go/
  VERSION  LICENSE  PATENTS  README.md
  api/  doc/  lib/  misc/  src/  test/
  bin/{go,gofmt}                        # plan9/$objtype binaries
  pkg/tool/plan9_$objtype/{compile,link,asm,vet,cgo,...}
  pkg/include/
```

## Status

- **plan9/amd64**: supported upstream. This build also includes the
  deadline-handling and `tcpsplice` improvements made while bringing up
  arm64.
- **plan9/arm64**: new port. See the merge-pending
  [Gerrit CL 719643](https://go-review.googlesource.com/c/go/+/719643).
- **9front kernel**: this Go release expects a 9front kernel containing
  the `tcpsplice`-close race fix
  (`bypeerclosed` field in `Tcpctl`, handled in `tcpsetstate` and
  `tcpclose`).
  A pre-patched 9front kernel source tarball can be requested separately.
